{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ConditionalCorollaries","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ConditionalCorollaries","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ConditionalClasses"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_rogue_zero_cost_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_rogue_zero_cost_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L208-L214","doc":"**Conditional rogue-zero cost bound**: under Aubin-Lions +\nblow-up, the rogue-zero energy cost `E(δ) = δ²/ε ≥ 0` for\n`δ : ℝ` and `ε > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_enstrophy_cube_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_enstrophy_cube_bound","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L191-L206","doc":"**Enstrophy cube bound**: every non-negative enstrophy `Z ≥ 0` satisfies\n`Z³ ≥ 0`.\n\n**This is UNCONDITIONAL and used to pretend otherwise.** It carried all\nfive q-NS class hypotheses while its proof is `pow_nonneg h_Z 3`, which\nuses none of them — `0 ≤ Z ^ 3` follows from `0 ≤ Z` alone. I flagged that\nin a note here and left the binders; a reviewer then flagged the same thing\non PR #6122, observing that it makes dependency tracking noisy and reads\nlater as a genuine conditional consequence. Two independent reads agreeing\nis enough: the binders are gone.\n\nVerified safe to drop: these corollaries have no external callers, so\nremoving hypotheses breaks nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_reeb_period_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_reeb_period_bound","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L181-L189","doc":"**Reeb-period bound**: `Ω · ε ≥ 0` for non-negative `Ω` and `ε`.\n\nUnconditional, and its class binders are dropped for the same reason as\n`qNS_enstrophy_cube_bound` above: the proof is `mul_nonneg` and used none\nof them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_cone_full_composition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_cone_full_composition","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L145-L179","doc":"**Full q-NS-cone composition** (all 5 classes).\n\nUntil 2026-08-30 this concluded that \"every conjectural existential field\nadmits a witness simultaneously\" — five existentials, all witnessed by\nzero, so the conjunction was provable with none of the hypotheses. Four of\nthe five conjuncts now say something the corresponding class is needed for:\na determined zero-energy compactness, an unbounded vorticity, the exponent's\nvalue, a null breakdown locus.\n\n**The fourth conjunct WAS the exception and no longer is.** It read\n`∃ r, 0 ≤ r` — satisfied by zero, the one place this composition stayed as\nweak as the whole thing used to be — because `BlowupYekutieli` had not been\nre-encoded. On 2026-08-30 that carrier was **replaced** by the upstream\nobstruction statement (`qou-88nf`), so all five conjuncts now need their\nclass. Note the replacement is not a strengthening of the old leg: a\nblow-up *rate* and obstruction-class *vanishing* are different\npropositions that shared a name.\n\nThe third conjunct read `α = 4/3` until 2026-08-30. That was a projection\nof a class field asserting a value the corpus calls open; both the field\nand this conjunct are gone (`qou-4670`). What replaces it is the\ndivergence consequence, which is derived rather than returned. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_critical_exponent_with_compactness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_critical_exponent_with_compactness","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L131-L143","doc":"**Three-class composition** (Aubin-Lions + critical + blow-up):\nthe enstrophy divergence survives combination with the Aubin-Lions and\nblow-up class hypotheses.\n\nThe conclusion changed with the class on 2026-08-30 (`qou-4670`); it used\nto be `3 * α = 4`, which the class no longer supports and which the\ncorpus does not assert. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_combined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qNS_combined","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L117-L129","doc":"**Two-class composition** (Aubin-Lions + blow-up): the compactness constant\nis pinned at zero energy *and* blow-up is a finite obstruction level.\n\nThe composition is the point — two class hypotheses used together without\ncircularity. **The asymmetry this docstring used to record is gone**: the\nYekutieli half produced an existential satisfied by zero until its carrier\nwas replaced on 2026-08-30 (`qou-88nf`), and now both halves derive\nsomething the hypothesis is needed for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.regularity_breakdown_subset_null","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.regularity_breakdown_subset_null","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L107-L115","doc":"**Every subset of the breakdown locus is null** — monotonicity of measure.\n\nUntil 2026-08-30 this concluded `∃ μ, 0 ≤ μ ∧ μ ≤ 0`, satisfied by `0`\nregardless. The class now asserts the locus is Lebesgue-null, so what\nfollows is a genuine statement about subsets of it. Bean `qou-m7a2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.blowup_yekutieli_iff_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.blowup_yekutieli_iff_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L93-L105","doc":"**Blow-up is a finite obstruction level** — the contrapositive half of\nsmoothness-as-lifting.\n\nUntil 2026-08-30 this concluded `∃ r, 0 ≤ r ∧ r ≤ 1 + 0`, satisfied by\n`r = 0` with or without the hypothesis. The class now states\n`smooth ↔ ∀ n, obstruction n = 0`, so what follows from it is the blow-up\ncharacterisation: failing to lift means some finite level obstructs. The\nproof is `not_forall` after rewriting, mirroring upstream\n`QOU.FluidDynamics.blowup_yekutieli`. Bean `qou-88nf`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.critical_exponent_enstrophy_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.critical_exponent_enstrophy_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L63-L91","doc":"**The enstrophy is unbounded near `q = 1`** — a consequence of the\ncritical-exponent conjecture.\n\nThree states on one day, and the middle one is the instructive failure.\n\n1. It concluded `(3 * 4 : ℕ) = 12` — true by `rfl` with or without the\n   hypothesis, so the `[CriticalExponent]` binder was decorative\n   (`qou-93hu`).\n2. It concluded `3 * α = 4`, from a class field typed `α = 4/3`. That\n   cleared the *shape* defect and inherited a worse one from the class:\n   **`4/3` is not a result the corpus holds.** `p2-critical-exponent.md`\n   offers it as one of two heuristic values under two named turbulence\n   closures and says the true exponent is open. So this theorem derived an\n   arithmetic identity from a fabricated premise — the derivation was\n   sound and the premise was not (`qou-4670`).\n3. Now: the class asserts divergence, and what follows from it is\n   unboundedness. `M` is arbitrary, so this is not satisfiable by any\n   bounded enstrophy, and it uses the hypothesis at `ε = 1`.\n\nNote the conclusion drops the neighbourhood. That is deliberate: the\nlocalisation is what makes the *hypothesis* strong, and a consequence is\nfree to be weaker. The `1 < q` conjunct is kept so the statement stays in\nthe q-NS regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ns_counterexample_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ns_counterexample_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L51-L61","doc":"**The vorticity is unbounded** — a consequence of blow-up.\n\nUntil 2026-08-30 this concluded `∃ T, 0 ≤ T` — \"there exists a non-negative\nreal\" — which needs no hypothesis at all. The class now asserts divergence,\nso what follows from it is that no bound holds. Bean `qou-5nj1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qAubinLions_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qAubinLions_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L42-L49","doc":"**Compactness is monotone in the energy bound** — the substantive half of\nlinearity: more available energy never yields a smaller constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qAubinLions_zero_energy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qAubinLions_zero_energy","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ConditionalCorollaries.lean#L30-L40","doc":"**Compactness vanishes at zero energy** — a consequence of linearity.\n\nUntil 2026-08-30 this concluded `∃ K, 0 ≤ K ∧ K ≤ 2 · 0`, i.e. that some\nnon-negative real is `≤ 0`, which is true of `0` with or without the\nhypothesis. The class now says `K` is linear in the energy, so the\nzero-energy value is *determined* rather than merely bounded, and the proof\nhas to use the hypothesis to get it. Bean `qou-3ytx`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}